# Reassigning a binding to an incompatible type rejected

Verifies a `let` binding keeps its declared type across assignments. Reassigning
a string binding to an integer binding is rejected even though the target
binding itself is mutable.

>>> source
let value: int = 10
let other: string = "x"
value = other

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: type mismatch: binding `value` expects `int64`, expression produces `string` at Span { start: 52, end: 57 }

<<< exit
1
